# Keeps the build context small. Everything listed here would otherwise be
# uploaded to the daemon on every build, land inside the image via `COPY .`,
# and invalidate the layer cache whenever it changed.
#
# Patterns are matched against the whole path from the context root, and `*`
# does not cross a `/`. Anything that can appear in a subdirectory therefore
# needs a `**/` prefix to be excluded everywhere rather than only at the root.

# Virtual environments. The image builds its own at /venv.
**/.venv/
**/venv/

# Version control and CI metadata
.git/
.gitattributes
.github/

# Python bytecode and packaging artifacts
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[codz]
**/*$py.class
**/*.so
**/*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Tool caches
**/.cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# Test and coverage output
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/coverage.xml
**/htmlcov/
reports/

# Editors and local agent config
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
.claude/

# Local environment files and shell history
**/.env
**/*.env
**/.bash_history
